10 But how thoſe things,
which Ariſtotle bringeth, doo agrée with the holie ſcriptures, we may eaſilie perceiue. Firſt he ſaith, that this opinion, as touching the groſſer ſort of pleaſures, is the opinion of manie, and that of the vulgar ſort of men. Which alſo Chriſt taught, affirming that the waie of perdition is large,
and manie doo go that waie. He addeth moreouer, that they which iudge this, are
〈 in non-Latin alphabet 〉, that is, moſt burdenſome. And in Eſaie we knowe, that it was ſaid to wicked Ahaz;
Is it a ſmall matter vnto you to be greeuous vnto men? Ariſtotle calleth them bond-ſlaues. And the Lord ſaid;
He that dooth ſinne, is the ſeruant of ſinne. Alſo Peter ſaid;
Euerie man is his ſeruant,
of whom he is ouercome. Ariſtotle ſaith, that they chooſe a beaſtlie life. And we haue it in the Pſalmes; Man, when he ſhould be in honour,
is compared vnto the brute beaſts, and is made like vnto them. Alſo
Ieremie;
Euerie man neigheth at his neighbours wife. And againe in the pſalme; Be ye not like horſſe and mule,
in whom there is no vnderſtanding. They which ſo thinke (ſaith the philoſopher) doo defend themſelues by the authoritie of princes, which liue after the maner of Sardanapalus. Neither dooth this diſagrée with the holie ſcriptures, wherein we read, that ſuch in a maner were the people, as were the kings whom they had.
And in
Oſea we reade; Such people, ſuch prieſt. In the Prouerbs, the 29. chapter; When the wicked ſhall beare rule, tranſgreſſion ſhall be multiplied. And in the Goſpels as touching Herod,
when the wiſe men came to Ieruſalem, we find that not onlie hée himſelfe was troubled, but alſo the whole citie with him. Laſtlie, it is concluded, that in theſe groſſer ſort of pleaſures cannot be repoſed the chéefeſt good. Which alſo the Apoſtle confirmeth to the Corinthians;
Meate for the bellie, and the bellie for meate, God ſhall deſtroie both the one and the other. And Chriſt himſelfe ſpeaking of the pleaſure of procreation;
In the regeneration they neither marrie wiues, nor are married, but they ſhall be like vnto the angels.
